      <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
        <tr valign="middle"> 
          <td colspan="2" height="30" background="newsheader.jpg"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><b><font size="5">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;SoF Attacks Chardok! (and vice versa)</font></b></font></td>
        </tr>
        <tr bgcolor="#330033"> 
          <td width="60%"><font size="2"><i><font face="Verdana">by <A href="javascript:createWindow('memberdetails.asp?id=1','profile','scrollbars,width=550,height=500')"><font color=yellow>Falqour Thornwalker</font></a></font></i></font></td>
          <td width="40%"> 
            <div align="right"><font size="2"><b>Posted: 12/1/2001 3:41:11 PM</b></font></div>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr> 
          <td colspan="2">
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><B><table width=100%><tr valign=top><td width=10%><img src="../newscaps/prince-magiq1sm.jpg"></td><td width=80%><font face=Verdana size=2 color=white><b>It was a bumpy ride, but in the end, it proved to be worth it. The guild is one step closer now to an Enchanter class epic weapon, a prized commodity, to be sure.<p>Congratulations go out to our very own Magiq Blueberry, for that ugly head now rotting in his backpack!</b></font></td><td width=10%><div align=right><img src="../newscaps/prince-magiq5sm.jpg"></div></td></tr></table>                  </B></font><P>
<font face="Verdana" size="2"><div align="right"><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/prince-magiq1.jpg" width="450" height="363" align="right"><font color="#FFFFFF">The Spirit of Fire Expeditionary Regulars conducted a daring raid on the Sarnak central command, a dank and smelly hole that the inhabitants refer to as CHARDOK, located deep within the Burning Woods. Their mission: Bring back the head of the Overking of the dreaded Di`Zok Brood, as well as the head of the Prince of Chardok.</font></font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF">Because of the many complications that arose, the mission was in interesting experience, to say the least. After starting a bit later then planned, the SoF Battlehoard made their way through the main gate of the underground city, making short work of the perimeter guard that defended the Di`Zok Royalty. We were making steady progress, when a certain monk who shall remain nameless, (it was Charisi) decided to alert the entirety of the Di`Zok defense force to our presence. The front lines were broken by no less then 15 or 20 bloodthirsty Sarnak warriors who quickly laid waste to our Expeditionary Regulars.</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF">It was a minor setback, though. Elite forces from the Crusaders of Plilo reinforced our position, and we were able recover fairly quickly. Shortly after I returned to life, I was dismayed to find once again that our presence had been discovered! I was barely able to escape, as Lucane valiantly fought off an advancing wave of Sarnaks, and in the process, lost his own life. Lucane will be missed. Er, wait, we brought him back to life.. So, no biggy.</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/prince-magiq3.jpg" width="450" height="338" align="left">After recovering a second time, we made our way to the inner sanctum of Chardok where we advanced first on the Prince, who proved to be little problem for us. After the short battle was complete, the head of this vile creature was awarded to an Enchanter in the ranks of the Crusaders. It would be about 2 hours before another Prince of Chardok was to be born, so, we decided to head over to the Overking and pay him a visit.</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF">Unfortunately, by the time we got to the staging area for our battle with the Overking, once again, the entire area was alerted to our presence, and another 20 of Chardok's best descended upon us. After a particularly one-sided battle, the SoF Regulars lay dead. One of our Clerics was able to escape the conflagration, and returned to piece together the broken bodies of our troops. Thanks again, Rezzme!</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF">At this point, with a total of 3 wipeouts thus far, our force's morale was at an all-time low. We were tired, bloody, and deep within enemy territory. It was decided, after much debate, that the mission should be scrubbed. Our main goal, the death of the Overking, would have to wait for another day. Our raid leader, Haletma, was understandably disappointed, as were the rest of us. But, we were able to rally our forces enough to trudge back to the Prince's throne and kill him a second time.</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/prince-magiq5.jpg" width="450" height="300" align="right">Magiq Phaze (Blueberry!), an Enchanter of the highest caliber, happily scooped up the ugly head to add to his collection. This head will prove invaluable in obtaining his Epic Weapon, a device that we will come to appreciate on future ventures.</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF">It was truly inspiring to see how, despite all our setbacks, most of us stayed till the very end to see our good friend Magiq get his reward. I'd personally like to thank everyone who participated on this raid.</font></p><p align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="4" color="#FFFFFF">And though we were unable to kill the Overking on this outing, I'm sure Chardok has not heard the last from the Spirit of Fire.</font></p><p align="center"> </p><p align="center"> </p><p align="center"><img src="http://www.sofeq.com/newscaps/prince-magiq4.jpg" width="574" height="115"></p></div>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       </font>
</td>
        </tr>
